    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="2.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 2.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="308" ed="#liebermann"/>And we beodað<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.oe.16"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man Cristene men for ealles to lytlu<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.oe.17"/></hi> huru to deaþe né forræde; ac elles geræde man friðlice steora folce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.oe.1-3"/> to þearfe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.oe.2-2"/> ⁊ ne forspille<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.oe.3"/> for<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.oe.4-2"/> lytlum Godes handgeweorc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.oe.5-2"/> ⁊ his agenne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.oe.6-2"/> ceap, þe he deore<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.oe.7-2"/> gebohte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="308" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ we forbeodað<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.oe.4"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man Cristene m<hi rend="italic">en</hi> for ealles to lytlum huru to deaðe ne forrǽde; ac elles gerǽde man friðlice steora folce to ðearfe, ⁊ ne forspille man for lytlum Godes handgeweorc ⁊ his agene ceap, ðe he deore gebohte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="308" ed="#liebermann"/>And we beodað, þæt man Cristene menn for ealles to lythum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.oe.6-3"/> huru to deaðe ne forræde; ac elles geræde man friðlice steora folce to ðærfe ⁊ ne forspille for litlu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> Godes handgeweorc ⁊ his agenne ceap, þe he deope<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.oe.1-4"/> gebohte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.1" corresp="#wit-d-frags"><pb n="308" ed="#liebermann"/>[2, 1] And witena gerædnes is, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man Cristene m<hi rend="italic">en</hi> for ealles to litlu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> huru to deaðe ne forræde; ac elles geræde man friðlice steora folce to ðearfe ⁊ ne forspille for litlum Godes handgeweorc ⁊ his agenne ceap, þe he deore gebohte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="2.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="309" ed="#liebermann"/>Prohibemus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.oe.7"/>, ne Christianus aliquis pro<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.oe.8"/> penitus parua ré saltem ad mortem seducatur (id<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.oe.9"/> est condempnetur aut preiudicetur); sed exquiratur pro necessitate populi iusticia pacificans, nec<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.oe.1-2"/> (ne) pro leui ré dispereat opus manuum Dei et suum ipsius pretium, quod profunde redemit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.1" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="309" ed="#liebermann"/>Interdicimus etiam, ne pro parua re Christiani morti tradantur, scilicet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.oe.12"/> pro latrocinio aut pro talibus rebus, sed alio modo corrigantur, propter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.oe.1-5"/> alios, ne culpę inulte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.oe.2-3"/> remaneant.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="2.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="309" ed="#liebermann"/>[2, 1] Interdicimus, ne quis quemquam pro modico admisso morte condempnet, set pocius discernatur pacifica correctio populo ad commodum, neque pro modico manuum Dei creatura eiusque proprius mercatus, quem care emit, deterreatur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="2a.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="176" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ we forbeodað<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_2-1.robnote.fn.1"/> þæt man Cristene men for ealles to lytlum huru to deaðe ne forrǽde, ac elles gerǽde man friðlice steora folce to ðearfe ⁊ ne forspille m<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_2-1.robnote.fn.2"/>an for lytlum Godes handgeweorc ⁊ his agene ceap ðe he deo<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_2-1.robnote.fn.3"/>re gebohte.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="254" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And we forbeodað þæt man Cristene men for ealles to lytlum huru to deaþe ne forræde; ac elles geræde man friðlice steora folce to þearfe and ne forspille for lytlum Godes handgeweorc and his agenne ceap, þe he deore gebohte.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="309" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wir gebieten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.de.1"/> (verbieten <hi rend="italic">B</hi>; Beschluss der Witan ist <hi rend="italic">D</hi>), dass man christliche Menschen für gar zu Geringes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.de.2"/> wenigstens nicht zum Tode verdamme; sondern anderweitig bestimme man [Leben] schonende Strafen, dem Volke zum Nutzen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_2-1.lnote.de.3"/>, und vernichte nicht um Geringes Gottes Händewerk und sein eigen Gut, das er theuer erkauft hat.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And we command (forbid, B; it is the decision of the witan, D) that Christian people are at least not to be condemned to death for all too small [offences]; but let [life-]sparing punishments be decided on instead, for the benefit of the people, and let God's handiwork and his own property, which he bought dearly (deeply, A), not be destroyed for small [offences].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_2-1.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="177" ed="#robertson"/>And we forbid the practice of condemning Christian people to death for very trivial offences. On the contrary, merciful punishments<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_2-1.robnote.n.2"/> shall be determined upon for the public good, and the handiwork of God and the purchase which he made at a great price<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_2-1.robnote.n.3"/> shall not be destroyed for trivial offences.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="255" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And we forbid Christians to be sentenced to death for entirely too little; instead, merciful penalties are to be established for the good of the people, and so that God’s handiwork, which he paid for himself at a high cost, not be destroyed because of petty crimes.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="309, 311"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_10">VI Atr 10</ref>; <ref target="clause:VIAtr_10-1">VI Atr 10.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 10 | Vgl. VI Atr. 10, 1</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_40">Leis Wl 40</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="357"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_10">VI Atr 10–10.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 2:1: Cn 1018 5  VI Atr 10-10:1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="357"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-013">Cn 1018 5</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 2:1: Cn 1018 5  VI Atr 10-10:1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="409"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_40">Leis Wl 40</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">G writes ‘forspille’ twice (the first later struck). A's ‘deope’ is a synonym of ‘deore’, also in Quadr.'s source. Liebermann compares VI Atr 10, 10.1.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 309, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
